I go back to customer service.
The shop assistant looks at me.
"And?"
"Does it fit better?" she asks.
"Yes, much better," I say.
"It is a little bigger than the other shirt."
"Great, then I will exchange that now," she says.
She takes the T-shirt and my receipt.
She types something into the computer.
"There, all done," the shop assistant says.
"Here is your new receipt."
"I wish you a nice weekend."
"Thank you, to you too!" I answer.
I pack the yellow T-shirt into my backpack.
Then I walk out of the shop.
Outside it is wonderfully warm.
I get on my bicycle.
Now I am finally ready for the Berlin summer.
